      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not waiting for the wreck; you are the wreck waiting to be rebuilt, and the moment you stop fighting is not the end, it is the beginning of the process. The shame is not a permanent state, but a temporary fog that clears when you take one small, deliberate step toward something new. Your friends and neighbors will not see a joke, but they will eventually see a person who has survived the fall and is now learning how to stand again. The descent is not the only thing left; the climb is the only thing that matters, and you are already on the path to it.",
